request.user_message:
Abstract the following semantic predicate cluster into exactly one reusable predicate.

Cluster ID:
binary-005

Cluster Arity:
2

Cluster Members:
[
  {
    "name": "ELIMINATES_EXPLANATION_WITH_CONTRARY_EVIDENCE",
    "definition": "The reasoning discards a candidate explanation for an observed situation because identifiable content of an observation contradicts a condition that the explanation requires.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning node rejecting the candidate explanation."
      },
      {
        "name": "observation",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation whose content contradicts the rejected explanation."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning names or clearly refers to a candidate explanation it discards.",
      "The reasoning cites identifiable observation content that conflicts with what that explanation would require, such as an empty listing contradicting a stash hypothesis or a clean status contradicting an uncommitted-changes hypothesis."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning narrows possibilities without stating what rules a candidate out.",
      "The observation is compatible with the discarded explanation or unrelated to it.",
      "What is discarded is a candidate solution or artifact rather than an explanation for the observed situation."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "SELECTS_TARGET_AMONG_CANDIDATES",
    "definition": "The reasoning identifies which of several comparable candidate items is the one relevant to the task, justifying the choice with discriminating attributes visible in an observation rather than by position, recency, or surface similarity.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning node comparing the candidates and identifying the relevant one."
      },
      {
        "name": "observation",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation exposing the discriminating attributes of the candidates."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "At least two comparable candidate items are distinguished in the reasoning.",
      "The selection is justified by at least one discriminating attribute visible in the observation, such as provenance, authorship, timestamp, or creation context.",
      "The reasoning concludes that one candidate is the item relevant to the task."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "Only one candidate is considered, so no discrimination is needed.",
      "A candidate is chosen by position, recency, or guess without cited discriminating evidence.",
      "The cited discriminating attribute is not actually present in the observation."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "DISMISSES_CANDIDATE_AS_UNINFORMATIVE",
    "definition": "The reasoning rejects or deprioritizes an inspected artifact or information source as a source of useful information because its observed content appears placeholder, random, unreadable, or otherwise uninformative.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "dismissal_reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning node explicitly characterizing the candidate as uninformative or deprioritizing it."
      },
      {
        "name": "content_observation",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation showing the candidate's content or metadata that makes it appear uninformative."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The observation shows content that can reasonably be judged dummy, random, unreadable, or otherwise lacking useful information.",
      "The reasoning explicitly characterizes that candidate as a dummy, random data, noise, or otherwise not useful, or deprioritizes it in favor of another candidate."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning merely notes uncertainty or unusual content while continuing to treat the same candidate as a primary source for the same kind of information.",
      "The reasoning reinterprets the same content as a useful artifact of a different type rather than dismissing the candidate.",
      "The observation contains no content or metadata supporting the dismissal.",
      "The reasoning does not actually reject or deprioritize the candidate."
    ]
  }
]

Previously Generated Predicate Names:
["CONFIGURES_EVENT_DRIVEN_AUTOMATION", "PREVENTS_SELF_CAUSED_ADVERSE_EFFECTS_THROUGH_CORRECTIVE_ACTION", "EVALUATES_CANDIDATE_AGAINST_ENUMERATED_CONSTRAINTS_OR_SCENARIOS", "RESOLVES_EVALUATED_CANDIDATE_ELEMENTS_TO_SINGLE_RESULT", "INTERPRETS_REQUIREMENTS_FOR_ACTION_ADMISSIBILITY", "INITIATES_DETACHED_ASYNCHRONOUS_EXECUTION", "REPORTS_ABSENT_OR_UNAVAILABLE_CAPABILITY", "IDENTIFIES_SPECIFIC_POTENTIAL_FAILURE_MODE", "ASSESSES_COMPETING_ACCOUNTS_OF_SAME_OBSERVATION", "ESTABLISHES_EVIDENCE_GROUNDED_TASK_OUTCOME_REFERENCE", "FORMULATES_STRUCTURED_OPERATIVE_ACCOUNT", "SPECIFIES_TARGET_LINKED_CONCRETE_MEANS", "GROUNDS_COMPUTATIONAL_ASSESSMENT_IN_QUANTITATIVE_ANALYSIS", "ANTICIPATES_PROSPECTIVE_VERIFICATION", "DELIMITS_MODIFICATION_AND_RESIDUAL_ARTIFACT_SCOPE", "IDENTIFIES_DEFICIENCY_OR_INCOMPLETENESS", "REPRODUCES_SPECIFIED_PROCEDURE_OR_OPERATION_ORDER", "IMPLEMENTS_LIMITATION_RESPONSIVE_ALTERNATIVE_APPROACH", "EXECUTES_REASONED_REMOVAL_OF_UNWANTED_STATE"]

Read every member's complete definition, ordered parameters, assertion conditions, and exclusion conditions. Identify the common underlying behavioral mechanism and generate exactly one complete predicate following the system instructions. The new predicate must preserve the cluster arity. Use a unique predicate name that does not conflict with previously generated predicate names. Return only the complete five-field JSON predicate.

message.content:
{
  "name": "RESOLVES_CANDIDATE_STATUS_FROM_OBSERVED_EVIDENCE",
  "definition": "The reasoning uses identifiable content of an observation as grounds for resolving the status of a candidate explanation, target item, artifact, or information source relative to the task: selecting it as the relevant, valid, or useful candidate; eliminating it because the observation contradicts a condition it requires; or rejecting or deprioritizing it as uninformative. The conclusion is justified by discriminating, contradictory, or disqualifying observed content rather than by candidate position, recency, surface similarity, guess, or unsupported assertion.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "reasoning",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "description": "The reasoning node that compares, validates, eliminates, selects, rejects, or deprioritizes a candidate on the basis of observed content."
    },
    {
      "name": "observation",
      "type": "observation",
      "description": "The observation providing the discriminating, contradictory, or uninformative content used to resolve the candidate's status."
    }
  ],
  "assertion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning refers to at least one candidate explanation, target item, artifact, or information source and concludes a resolved status for it: selected as relevant, valid, or useful; eliminated as contradicted; or rejected or deprioritized as uninformative.",
    "The reasoning cites identifiable observation content as the basis for that status, such as a discriminating attribute among multiple candidates, content conflicting with a condition required by the candidate, or content indicating placeholder, random, unreadable, or otherwise uninformative material.",
    "When multiple comparable candidates are considered, the observation exposes at least one attribute that differentiates the selected candidate from the others or exposes disqualifying content for a rejected candidate.",
    "The resolved status follows from the cited observed content rather than solely from candidate position, recency, surface similarity, or unsupported preference."
  ],
  "exclusion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning only notes uncertainty, unusual content, or a possible candidate without selecting, eliminating, rejecting, or deprioritizing it.",
    "The observation is compatible with the candidate's required condition and does not indicate uninformative content, yet the reasoning rejects or deprioritizes the candidate.",
    "The reasoning selects a candidate solely by position, recency, surface similarity, or guess without citing discriminating observation content.",
    "The discriminating or disqualifying attribute cited by the reasoning is not actually present in the observation.",
    "The reasoning performs an operation on a candidate without resolving whether that candidate is relevant, valid, useful, contradicted, or uninformative."
  ]
}

